200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (Modern software depends on thousands of open-source packages, yet users generally trust that a published binary was actually built from the public source code. A compromised maintainer account, build server, or release pipeline can silently introduce malicious changes into widely distributed software. The 2024 XZ Utils incident demonstrated how a sophisticated supply-chain attack can remain hidden inside a trusted software ecosystem.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 78 0 R
/E (The core problem is that users have little practical way to independently verify that a released artifact actually corresponds to its claimed source.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
